  "interpretation": [
    "The objective retains the determinant on the 20-dimensional identifiable span of a 21-column fiducial spectral information proxy after SVD whitening.",
    "Each channel contributes a Jacobian row divided by its existing per-pixel MJy/sr sensitivity.",
    "Local shape columns use unit reference amplitudes; each nonzero column is normalized before the SVD. Global shape columns include the fiducial physical amplitudes.",
    "The CRR spectral template is explicitly included, so its frequency structure participates in every removal decision.",
    "The 50 and 545 GHz amplitude-reference bands and the 2000 GHz endpoint are retained exactly.",
    "At least eight channels remain in each of four equal-frequency intervals; this limits clustering around a few spectral features.",
    "This is a deterministic backward greedy heuristic for the declared fiducial model and current free parameters, not a globally optimal experimental design.",
    "The spectral proxy does not include pixel morphology, local spectral-parameter priors, masking correlations, nonlinear posterior geometry or model mismatch. Its marginal error ratios are not spatial posterior forecasts.",
    "The per-pixel sensitivity convention is the same at NSIDE 128 and 64. An overall pixel-count factor does not change this spectral ranking.",
    "No map, sensitivity, original channel ID or export manifest is changed. Parameter files remap the selected original IDs to contiguous analysis IDs.",
    "The primary CMB anisotropy amplitude and global DeltaT have exactly the same SED. No artificial spectral distinction is introduced; their common spectral direction is counted once by the SVD.",
    "Spatial morphology and the CMB harmonic prior supply information beyond this spectral design proxy. They must be included by the actual spatial component-separation model.",
    "For a rank-deficient feature basis, spectral_proxy_marginal_std_inflations describe minimum-norm coordinates projected onto the identifiable spectral span. They are not finite unconstrained uncertainties for the original degenerate parameters.",
    "Free-free uses the Draine Gaunt-factor amplitude-plus-electron-temperature response declared by the export, rather than a free power-law index."
  ],
